ation during the relevant years:\nL161: \nL162:   * Millennials in 2022 (ages 26 to 41 — the latest available)\nL163:   * Generation Xers in 2007 (ages 27 to 42)\nL164:   * Baby boomers in 1989 (ages 25 to 43)\nL165: The SCF is conducted in three-year intervals. The data provided was adjusted to 2022 dollars by the Federal Reserve.\nL166: \nL167: Cumulative income is the sum of median income for people in the relevant age group (25 to 34) from the U.S. Census Bureau Current Population Survey Annual Social and Economic Supplements, reported and adjusted to 2023 dollars in “Table P-10. Age — All Peoples (Both Sexes Combined) by Median and Mean Income: 1974 to 2023” (the latest available).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHUD Archives: HUD and Census Bureau Report New Residential Sales in July 2024 (https://archives.hud.gov/news/2024/pr24-218.cfm)\nciteturn76view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://archives.hud.gov/news/2024/pr24-218.cfm\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 44\nL0:  | 【0†Home】 | Contact Us (webmanager@hud.gov) | 【1†A to Z】\nL1: 【2†Image: HUD Archives】\nL2: \nL3: 【3†Image】  |\nL4: 【3†Image】  |\nL5: \nL6: ## HUD Archives: News Releases\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 【3†Image】  |\nL11: 【4†Image: HUD Seal】 【5†Image: Census Bureau Seal】\nL12: U.S. Dept. of Housing and Urban Development\nL13: Office of Public Affairs\nL14: (202) 708-0685\nL15: August 23, 2024 U.S. Census Bureau\nL16: Economic Indicators Division\nL17: (301) 763-5160\nL18: \nL19: * * *\nL20: ### HUD and Census Bureau Report New Residential Sales in July 2024\n"
